status.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The nested spec repo. It is a separate git repository with its own remote, so the product's
# history never carries planning artifacts.
.specs/

# Agent scratch state. Never committed, and named explicitly rather than left to a global
# ignore, so the rule holds on a machine that has no global ignore at all. An earlier version
# of this file deliberately re-included it so the dashboard could draw a progress bar from the
# ledger; the bar is not worth putting one agent's working notes into a repository that is
# meant to be read by other people.
.superpowers/

# CLAUDE.md is commonly ignored by a global ignore file, and this project is meant to be cloned:
# its ## Task Workflow section is what resolve-task-paths reads to find the PRD, the specs and the
# tasks. Without this re-include the file stays on the author's disk and every clone gets a
# project whose pipeline resolves nothing, which is the failure this repository exists to teach.
!CLAUDE.md
